    oe:questionText "What is the recommended first-line pharmacological treatment for Peptic Ulcer Disease?"^^xsd:string ;
    oe:answerText "In the US, peptic ulcer disease affects 1% of the population and approximately 54 000 patients are admitted to the hospital annually for bleeding peptic ulcers. Approximately 10% of patients presenting with upper abdominal pain in a primary care setting have a peptic ulcer as the cause of their symptoms."^^xsd:string ;
